"""Add distinct decision tools to three legacy procurement guides."""
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
SECTIONS = {
 'building-a-wholesale-product-list': '''<h2>Use a line-item RFQ that can be reconciled</h2><p>Give every requested item a line number. Record the catalogue name, requested presentation, quantity, whether substitution is permitted and any unresolved question. Ask the supplier to reply against those same line numbers. A quoted quantity should refer to a clearly defined unit: a box, vial or syringe must not be treated as interchangeable.</p><ul><li>Line 01: exact item and presentation; requested quantity; unit definition to confirm.</li><li>Substitution: not permitted unless separately approved in writing.</li><li>Availability: confirmed quantity, expected confirmation date or unavailable.</li><li>Commercial details: currency, quotation validity and charges included or excluded.</li></ul><h2>Example: compare quantity options without changing the product</h2><p>In a hypothetical request, a clinic asks for 10 and 25 boxes of the same item. The buyer should ask for two separately labelled options with the same presentation and destination. If one option uses a different pack configuration, the unit prices are not directly comparable. Record the number of saleable units only after the pack contents are confirmed; leave freight, tax and other unknown charges uncalculated until quoted.</p><h2>Control changes before confirming the order</h2><p>Number each revision of the request. If quantities change, ask for a replacement summary rather than relying on messages scattered through a conversation. Before payment, reconcile the final product list with the quotation, identify unresolved items and confirm who approves substitutions. Keep the accepted version for receiving checks.</p><p>Start with the <a href="../categories/dermal-fillers.html">dermal filler directory</a> or <a href="../categories/skin-boosters-pn.html">skin booster directory</a>, then read the <a href="shipping-aesthetic-products-internationally.html">shipment planning guide</a> before finalising the destination details.</p>''',
 'shipping-aesthetic-products-internationally': '''<h2>Separate the order record from the shipment record</h2><p>The order record identifies what was purchased. The shipment record identifies which items are in each parcel, who holds the tracking reference and how an exception will be reported. Ask for carton identifiers and a packing list that can be reconciled to the accepted quotation. These records support receiving checks; they do not establish import eligibility or prove that a product was handled correctly.</p><h2>Agree an exception workflow before dispatch</h2><ul><li>Who monitors tracking and contacts the carrier when movement stops?</li><li>Who supplies additional documents requested during import review?</li><li>How should the receiver report a damaged carton or an item mismatch?</li><li>Which records should be retained while the issue is investigated?</li></ul><p>A hypothetical two-carton delivery can arrive on separate days. The receiver should reconcile each carton separately and mark the second as outstanding rather than recording the entire order as complete. A tracking scan confirms a carrier event, not the condition or identity of every item inside.</p><h2>Review handling requirements by item</h2><p>Do not infer storage conditions from a broad product category or from another brand. Request the applicable manufacturer instructions for the exact presentation and discuss the proposed route with the supplier. If handling evidence is needed, define what evidence is available before purchase. A parcel photograph cannot demonstrate temperature history.</p><p>Keep affected items separate when there is an unresolved condition concern and seek the appropriate professional assessment before use. Record the time received, parcel condition and discrepancy against the packing list. Consult <a href="../shipping.html">HANSEONG shipping support</a> with your exact list, and use the <a href="building-a-wholesale-product-list.html">RFQ preparation guide</a> to avoid missing destination information.</p>''',
 'wholesale-dermal-filler-malaysia-b2b-buyers-guide': '''<h2>A supplier scorecard with evidence fields</h2><p>Score the supplier against evidence rather than impressions. For each criterion, record the question asked, the answer received, the supporting record and any unresolved point. A fast reply can earn a communication score, but it should not compensate for an unidentified product presentation or contradictory quotation.</p><ul><li>Product identity: can the quoted item be matched to an exact presentation?</li><li>Commercial clarity: are quantities, units, currency and exclusions stated?</li><li>Order control: are substitutions and changes subject to written acceptance?</li><li>Receiving support: is there a defined channel for reporting discrepancies?</li></ul><h2>For buyers evaluating supply into Malaysia</h2><p>Separate the supplier evaluation from the destination review. Before a transaction, identify the exact product, the purchasing entity and the party responsible for import arrangements. Ask the relevant local professional or importer to verify applicable requirements for that specific item. This guide does not confirm that a listed product is approved or available for supply into Malaysia.</p><p>Keep destination questions in a separate column of the scorecard. A supplier can communicate clearly while a proposed product or route remains unsuitable. Leave that item unresolved until the required evidence is available; do not treat catalogue presence or an attractive quotation as a substitute for destination checks.</p><h2>Use a pilot order to test the process</h2><p>If a pilot purchase is appropriate, define success before placing it: correct items, agreed quantities, reconciled documents and a usable communication record. Review the outcome before expanding the order. A successful pilot demonstrates performance on that transaction, not a guarantee for future orders.</p><p>Review the <a href="../categories/dermal-fillers.html">dermal filler catalogue directory</a> and prepare a <a href="building-a-wholesale-product-list.html">line-item wholesale request</a> before asking for a <a href="../contact.html">destination-specific quotation</a>.</p>'''
}

for slug, section in SECTIONS.items():
    path = ROOT / 'blog' / (slug + '.html')
    source = path.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
    marker = '<!-- BUYER_DECISION_TOOLS -->'
    if marker not in source:
        assert '</article>' in source
        source = source.replace('</article>', marker + section + '</article>', 1)
        path.write_text(source, encoding='utf-8')
print('Three buyer guides enriched')
